/-! ## The point group `D₆ₕ`

The molecular point group of benzene, `D₆ₕ`, is the direct product of the dihedral group `D₆`
(of order 12: six rotations `Cₙ` about the principal axis together with six twofold axes)
with the two element group generated by the inversion centre `i`.  It has order 24. -/

/-- The point group `D₆ₕ = D₆ × Cᵢ`, of order `24`. -/
abbrev D6h := DihedralGroup 6 × Multiplicative (ZMod 2)

instance : Fintype D6h := inferInstanceAs (Fintype (DihedralGroup 6 × Multiplicative (ZMod 2)))


lemma zmodPow_mul {n : ℕ} [NeZero n] {x : M} (hx : x ^ n = 1) (i j : ZMod n) :
    zmodPow x (i + j) = zmodPow x i * zmodPow x j := by
  unfold zmodPow
  rw [ZMod.val_add, pow_mod_of_pow_eq_one hx, pow_add]

